## Context
Author ruling, 2026-10-27 raid: mammoth-audit is a heavy measurement that belongs to the
harness-doctor's toolkit, not a public command. Today it ships as `bin/mammoth-audit` (a wrapper over
`scripts/mammoth-audit.py`, ticket 0876) and is projected to `~/.local/bin/idh-mammoth-audit` by
`adapters/projections.json`; `tests/test_mammoth_audit.py` runs it through that installed launcher.
Ticket 1249/1257 just defined `bin/` as curated public commands, which this does not fit.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `bin/mammoth-audit` and its `idh-mammoth-audit` projection are gone; `idh install` retires an
      existing `~/.local/bin/idh-mammoth-audit` link (test on a temporary HOME).
- [ ] Any scheduler or cron entry that runs it is removed or repointed, stated in the PR.
- [ ] `skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md` (or its references) names the audit as a doctor's measurement,
      called as `"$IDH_ROOT/scripts/mammoth-audit.py"`, with when to use it and its cost.
- [ ] `tests/test_mammoth_audit.py` exercises the script directly; the harness gate passes.
- [ ] Every public command in bin/ carries the `idh-` prefix (install-cron → idh-install-cron, snapshot → idh-snapshot,
      usage-report → idh-usage-report; `idh` itself stays); every caller, doc, test, projection and timer is updated
      (grep the whole repo); `idh install` retires the old unprefixed links it owns and never touches a user's own
      command of that name (test on a temporary HOME); bin/README states the prefix rule.

## Relevant files
bin/mammoth-audit, adapters/projections.json, scripts/mammoth-audit.py, tests/test_mammoth_audit.py,
skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md, bin/install-cron

Related: [[1257]], [[1249]].
